# T5 #3 regression — era boundary coincident with a new-era spring-forward, where the new era's
# standard offset is 1h SMALLER than the old era's. Reference `zic` makes the boundary itself the
# DST transition: the UT offset is continuous (+3 -> +3) but isdst flips 0->1 and the abbreviation
# goes to the DST form. The bug was a spurious 1h standard interval after the boundary. This is the
# generic shape of Europe/Moscow 1991 (3 R MSK/MSD -> 2 R EE%sT, both "Mar lastSun 02:00s").
Rule BS 1970 max - Mar lastSun 2:00s 1:00 D
Rule BS 1970 max - Oct lastSun 2:00s 0 S
Zone Test/BoundarySpring 3:00 BS CE%sT 1985 Mar lastSun 2:00s
			 2:00 BS EE%sT 1995
			 2:00 -  EET
